1
00:00:02,222 --> 00:00:07,207
The Life Of Muhammad ﷺ, Madinan Period Volume 2

2
00:00:07,805 --> 00:00:09,749
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki;

3
00:00:10,901 --> 00:00:15,291
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:16,146 --> 00:00:22,574
The Army went forth, this deliberation happened in an area in Jordan called, Ma'an(مَعان).

5
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:26,704
And now they are moving forward towards the plains of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

6
00:00:27,006 --> 00:00:28,815
Mu'tah(مَؤتَة) is also in Jordan.

7
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:32,748
With this army was a new Muslims, Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه.

8
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:37,693
Remember we just talked about him, we said that he became Muslim in Khaybar(خيبر).

9
00:00:38,768 --> 00:00:43,662
So, Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) tells us his experience, in this battle.

10
00:00:44,123 --> 00:00:45,940
Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه said;

11
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:53,918
شَهِدْتُ مَؤته فَلَمَّا دَنَا مِنَّا الْمُشْرِكُوْنْ رَاَيْنَا مَا لَا قِبَلِ لاَحَد بِه

12
00:00:54,383 --> 00:01:00,184
 مِنَّ الْعُدَةْ وَالْسَلَاحْ وَالْكَرَاعْ وَالْدِيْبَاجْ وَالْحَرِيْر وَالْذَهَبْ فَبَرِقَ بَصَرِيْ

13
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:04,556
Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه said: I attended the Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

14
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:07,848
When the Mushrikeen(مشركين) came close to us.

15
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:18,920
We saw what no one could face; weapons, preparation, silk, gold, so my eye became dazzled.

16
00:01:19,568 --> 00:01:22,848
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه was a new Muslim

17
00:01:23,430 --> 00:01:26,914
and there's some things that a Muslim learns by experience.

18
00:01:26,938 --> 00:01:29,766
Sometimes, it's not all knowledge, sometimes it's experience.

19
00:01:30,387 --> 00:01:34,291
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) here remember, he's coming from a Jahiliyyah(جاهلية) background.

20
00:01:35,802 --> 00:01:42,438
An army of 3000 facing an army of 200,000 is something that you would find in no religion and no tradition.

21
00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:45,513
The Arab tribesmen cannot think about that

22
00:01:45,841 --> 00:01:51,121
and anybody coming from any other culture or tradition, it's something that is incomprehendible,

23
00:01:51,161 --> 00:01:54,530
 I mean why should we do this, this is death.

24
00:01:55,638 --> 00:01:58,273
Not only were the numbers fearsome.

25
00:01:58,726 --> 00:02:05,439
But now when they face the army, see because before it was news that they heard with their ears now they are seeing it.

26
00:02:05,472 --> 00:02:06,860
لَيْسَ الْخَبَر كَالْمُعَايْنَه

27
00:02:07,029 --> 00:02:08,784
Hearing something is not like seeing it.

28
00:02:09,234 --> 00:02:14,663
And then these armies, they played on the psychology of the, of the enemy,

29
00:02:15,084 --> 00:02:22,708
the looks, the show of force, they knew that, this plays an important role on demoralizing the enemy.

30
00:02:23,019 --> 00:02:27,377
So, they come in a show, probably there was, there were drums beating.

31
00:02:27,723 --> 00:02:30,375
And then Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) said;

32
00:02:30,486 --> 00:02:37,934
The preparation, and the weapons that we could see, and then the gold and the Debaaj(ديباج) and Hareer(حرير),

33
00:02:38,243 --> 00:02:44,124
 the silk and Deebaaj(ديباج) which is a thick cloth of silk that the army was dressed in

34
00:02:44,519 --> 00:02:47,945
all of this puts fear in the hearts of the enemy.

35
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:49,461
Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) said;

36
00:02:49,595 --> 00:02:51,035
 فَبَرِقَ بَصَرِيْ

37
00:02:51,527 --> 00:02:54,220
I became dazzled and Bareqa(فَبَرِقَ) is like lightning.

38
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:59,753
He said: My eyes were struck as if he was saying my eyes was struck with lightning.

39
00:03:00,472 --> 00:03:04,006
Was this confusion, was that fear, was it surprise.?

40
00:03:04,190 --> 00:03:07,280
Anyway it's something that could be seen on the face of Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره).

41
00:03:07,361 --> 00:03:09,678
Next to him was Thabit Bin Arqam(ثابت بن أرقم).

42
00:03:10,112 --> 00:03:13,154
Thabit Bin Arqam(ثابت بن أرقم) saw what was going on.

43
00:03:13,296 --> 00:03:15,073
He told Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره),

44
00:03:15,177 --> 00:03:16,949
كَاَنَّكَ تَرَى جَمُوْعًا كَثِيْرَةْ

45
00:03:17,187 --> 00:03:19,480
It seems that you are seeing a huge force.

46
00:03:19,734 --> 00:03:22,942
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) said, Yes definitely, I mean look at this.

47
00:03:23,368 --> 00:03:25,239
Are we supposed to fight these people.

48
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:33,542
Thabit Bin Arqam(ثابت بن أرقم) here, and this is the role of the senior Muslim handing down his experience to the new Muslim, to the junior,

49
00:03:33,772 --> 00:03:36,872
the old handing down the experience to the young.

50
00:03:37,649 --> 00:03:40,651
Thabit Bin Arqam(ثابت بن أرقم) is steeped in Islam.

51
00:03:41,572 --> 00:03:43,293
 He told Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره),

52
00:03:43,718 --> 00:03:48,717
قَالَ: إِنَّكَ لَمْ تَشْهَدْ مَعَنَا بَدْرًا، إِنَّا لَمْ نُنْصَرْ بِالْكَثْرًةْ

53
00:03:49,386 --> 00:03:55,113
You were not with us at Badr(بدر), we are not given victory through numbers.

54
00:03:56,004 --> 00:04:01,355
Here he's handing down to Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) a lesson that is learned by experience.

55
00:04:01,983 --> 00:04:04,224
You were not there at Badr(بدر).

56
00:04:04,518 --> 00:04:13,973
We Muslims, forget about the laws of nature, and war, that you had with you, in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية), forget about that.

57
00:04:14,204 --> 00:04:18,075
Now, you're Muslim it's a new world, we viewed the world differently.

58
00:04:18,227 --> 00:04:20,257
We Muslims see things differently.

59
00:04:20,352 --> 00:04:21,963
You were not there at Badr(بدر).

60
00:04:22,506 --> 00:04:25,692
Now, the numbers were at Badr(بدر) nothing like what we're talking about here.

61
00:04:25,809 --> 00:04:34,717
But at Badr(بدر), it was the first encounter, and then the Muslims saw the interference, through the soldiers of Allah,

62
00:04:34,876 --> 00:04:38,043
 they saw the angels come in and give them victory.

63
00:04:38,067 --> 00:04:43,814
It was not their numbers, the Muslims were little over 300 and the enemy was 1000.

64
00:04:43,838 --> 00:04:46,205
So, it was only three times the number.

65
00:04:46,387 --> 00:04:50,443
Here we're talking about 3000 against 200,000.

66
00:04:51,125 --> 00:04:54,020
So, it's a completely different thing But he's telling him

67
00:04:54,282 --> 00:04:58,871
that it's not numbers that give us victory, it is our trust in Allah.

68
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:05,046
وَمَا رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ رَمَىٰ

69
00:05:05,590 --> 00:05:08,576
These Ayaat(آيات) were revealed when.? After the Battle of Badr(بدر),

70
00:05:09,121 --> 00:05:11,993
it was not you, who fired, it is Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

71
00:05:12,317 --> 00:05:14,688
 وَمَا رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ رَمَىٰ

72
00:05:15,248 --> 00:05:17,306
And this is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي).

73
00:05:18,654 --> 00:05:25,397
The battle started, Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), the leader is ahead of the army, and not behind them.

74
00:05:25,876 --> 00:05:32,473
He's carrying the banner with courage, leading his army, giving them, example.

75
00:05:33,122 --> 00:05:37,387
He moved forth carrying the banner in his arms.

76
00:05:37,966 --> 00:05:39,766
And it says in the narration

77
00:05:40,053 --> 00:05:42,537
حَتَّى طَاشَ فِيْ رمَاحَ الْعَدُوّ

78
00:05:43,052 --> 00:05:46,653
Until he was lost among their lances.

79
00:05:47,155 --> 00:05:49,546
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) moved forward.

80
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:52,038
Until, you cannot see him anymore

81
00:05:52,061 --> 00:05:58,892
because he was lost in a sea of lances, spears covering him from every direction, stabbing him from every corner.

82
00:05:59,490 --> 00:06:01,697
Until, there was Zaid(زيد) no more.

83
00:06:02,157 --> 00:06:08,200
Then the banner was carried by Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه,

84
00:06:08,489 --> 00:06:11,533
who just came back from Abyssinia.

85
00:06:11,787 --> 00:06:14,339
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not keep him, next to him.

86
00:06:14,453 --> 00:06:18,117
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him to the army, sent him to battle.

87
00:06:18,605 --> 00:06:23,664
Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب) carried the banner and in the heat of the battle

88
00:06:23,968 --> 00:06:27,829
Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر إبن أبي طالب) felt that his horse is hindering him.

89
00:06:28,248 --> 00:06:30,713
So, he dismounted and he killed his horse.

90
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:37,094
And this was used as evidence for example by the Ah'naaf(أحناف),  Imam Abu Haneefah(امام ابوحنيفة)

91
00:06:37,598 --> 00:06:43,658
that you're allowed to kill your animal to prevent the enemy from taking advantage of it.

92
00:06:43,714 --> 00:06:49,706
Because the rule is that we should not kill an animal, wastefully.

93
00:06:49,794 --> 00:06:52,104
If you're not going to eat it, why kill that animal?

94
00:06:52,588 --> 00:06:59,717
But they use this as evidence if it is with the intention of preventing the enemy from making use of it, then it's allowed.

95
00:07:00,396 --> 00:07:05,153
So, Jafar(جعفر) he killed his horse and then he moved on foot,

96
00:07:06,415 --> 00:07:11,887
it is said that his right arm was cut, so he carried the banner with his left

97
00:07:11,927 --> 00:07:18,567
and that was cut, so then he held it, he hugged the banner with what was left from his arms,

98
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:22,181
 and then he was eventually killed

99
00:07:22,607 --> 00:07:27,728
and he was full of stabs from ahead of him and from behind him.

100
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:34,081
In Bukhari(بخاري) it says that Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) used to call him, the man of two wings.

101
00:07:34,686 --> 00:07:42,367
Because Allah replaced him, instead of his two arms which were which were cut off, Allah replaced him with two wings

102
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:46,538
after he died to fly in Jannah(جنة), wherever he wants.

103
00:07:47,398 --> 00:07:53,347
And then Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة) took over the Imarah(إمارة), the leadership of the army.

104
00:07:54,034 --> 00:07:57,044
He was handed a piece of meat to strengthen himself.

105
00:07:57,626 --> 00:08:00,302
So, he started eating from that piece of meat,

106
00:08:00,751 --> 00:08:07,749
and then he heard an uproar from a certain corner of the battlefield.

107
00:08:07,971 --> 00:08:08,805
He said;

108
00:08:08,854 --> 00:08:11,855
وَمَا زِلْتَ فِيْ هَذَا وَمَا زِلْتَ فِيْ الدُّنْيَا

109
00:08:12,109 --> 00:08:17,444
And you are still in this world and he jumped ahead and was killed Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

110
00:08:18,417 --> 00:08:23,784
Now, the three Umara'a(أمراء), the three leaders, who were appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ were killed.

111
00:08:24,369 --> 00:08:29,706
Thabit Bin Arqam رضي الله عنه, whom we just talked about he carried the banner and he said;

112
00:08:29,835 --> 00:08:33,032
Choose from among you, O Muslims, a leader to lead us.

113
00:08:33,259 --> 00:08:35,651
They said, you lead us, he said; No I won't.

114
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:39,800
So, they gave the banner to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and they said: You are our leader.

115
00:08:39,824 --> 00:08:43,898
So, it was the Muslims who appointed Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) they chose him to lead,

116
00:08:44,222 --> 00:08:49,157
and he was also a new Muslim and this is the first battle that he would lead.

117
00:08:49,910 --> 00:08:56,744
Rasool Allah ﷺ would receive the news through Jibreel عليه السّلام, when he was in Madina,

118
00:08:56,912 --> 00:09:01,780
he would receive the news from the battlefield in Jordan, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

119
00:09:01,894 --> 00:09:08,546
أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ زَيْدٌ فَأُصِيبَ ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ جَعْفَرٌ فَأُصِيبَ ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ ابْنُ رَوَاحَةَ فَأُصِيبَ

120
00:09:08,765 --> 00:09:13,222
 حَتَّى أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ  سَيْفٌ مِنْ سُيُوفِ اللَّهِ حَتَّى فَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ

121
00:09:13,254 --> 00:09:14,297
And this is in Al-Bukhari(ألبخاري).

122
00:09:14,565 --> 00:09:18,463
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: The banner was carried by Zaid(زيد), until he was killed,

123
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:21,633
and then it was carried by Jafar(جعفر), until he was killed

124
00:09:21,841 --> 00:09:25,554
and then it was carried by Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة), until he was killed,

125
00:09:25,683 --> 00:09:29,766
and then the banner was carried by a Sword from the Swords of Allah,

126
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:31,270
until Allah gave them victory.

127
00:09:31,697 --> 00:09:36,481
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was a sword of Allah and the Muslims need a sword of Allah.

128
00:09:36,641 --> 00:09:40,723
They needed a sword of Allah yesterday, and we need the sword from Allah today.

129
00:09:41,505 --> 00:09:47,868
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), he carried the banner and he was fighting, leading the Muslims,

130
00:09:48,333 --> 00:09:51,423
a new Muslim but the spirit of Islam was strong.

131
00:09:51,605 --> 00:09:53,401
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said;

132
00:09:53,481 --> 00:09:55,678
تَكَسّرَتْ فِي يَدَيْ تِسْعَةَ اَسْيَافْ

133
00:09:55,948 --> 00:09:58,377
Nine swords broke in my hand,

134
00:09:58,402 --> 00:10:00,851
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), what was Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) doing with those swords.

135
00:10:01,217 --> 00:10:04,281
He broke down nine swords, and then he said;

136
00:10:04,321 --> 00:10:10,307
 In the end only a broad sword, Yemeni broad sword survived with me.

137
00:10:10,709 --> 00:10:14,092
So, the question is not whether Khalid(خالد) can deal with the swords,

138
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:18,278
the question is whether the sword can handle Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

139
00:10:18,931 --> 00:10:24,988
Nine swords were broken in one day, on the enemies of Allah

140
00:10:25,289 --> 00:10:32,488
and only broad sword, the big piece of iron, Yemeni sword survived in his hand until the end of the day.

141
00:10:33,322 --> 00:10:38,425
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: About the three leaders of the army,

142
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:41,380
وَمَا يَسرُّهُمْ اَنَّهُمْ مَعَنَا

143
00:10:42,118 --> 00:10:45,300
And it would not please them to be with us.

144
00:10:45,914 --> 00:10:53,016
Zaid(زيد), Jafar(جعفر) and Abdullah Bin Rawaha(عبدالله بن رواحة), are happier in Aakhira(آخرة) then in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

145
00:10:53,395 --> 00:10:56,630
They don't want to come back with us, they're happy where they are.

146
00:10:58,110 --> 00:11:00,649
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), it is mentioned in one narration.

147
00:11:01,427 --> 00:11:04,539
He, at nightfall, when the fighting stopped.

148
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,832
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), what he was doing?

149
00:11:06,888 --> 00:11:11,746
He was doing a slow retreat, he doesn't want to do a fast retreat

150
00:11:11,778 --> 00:11:17,753
because then the enemy will take advantage of that and destroy the army.

151
00:11:18,174 --> 00:11:26,234
So, it was a slow retreat, they're holding on, and he was doing it slowly, until nightfall.

152
00:11:26,603 --> 00:11:29,950
He is trying to encourage the Muslims to hold on.

153
00:11:30,587 --> 00:11:35,350
At night what he did he switched the left flank to the right and the right to the left.

154
00:11:35,948 --> 00:11:40,314
So, when they woke up in the morning and the Romans saw, the army.

155
00:11:41,087 --> 00:11:46,028
So, the right flank of the Romans would see different people in front of them

156
00:11:46,485 --> 00:11:49,740
and the left flank of the Romans would see different people in front of them.

157
00:11:50,259 --> 00:11:54,185
They were deceived to believe that the Muslims received reinforcement's.

158
00:11:55,131 --> 00:12:03,009
So, they told themselves, If the Muslims were able to hold ground, when they were only 3000.

159
00:12:03,691 --> 00:12:08,522
What are they going to do today, after they have received reinforcements.?

160
00:12:08,823 --> 00:12:11,219
And this convinced the Romans to retreat.

161
00:12:11,778 --> 00:12:15,195
And this is the victory that Rasool Allah ﷺ is talking about in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

162
00:12:15,879 --> 00:12:18,143
This is the opening that Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

163
00:12:18,913 --> 00:12:19,950
فَفَتَحَ الله عَلَيْهَا

164
00:12:20,165 --> 00:12:25,210
When that happened and the Romans stopped, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), immediately retreated,

165
00:12:25,855 --> 00:12:28,255
with the army and they came back to Madina.

166
00:12:29,308 --> 00:12:34,618
Rasool Allah ﷺ visited the children of Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه

167
00:12:34,642 --> 00:12:37,537
the cousin of Rasool Ullah, the brother of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

168
00:12:38,042 --> 00:12:42,176
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told their mother, to bring the children.

169
00:12:42,379 --> 00:12:48,090
Asma(أسماء) said: I have already cleaned them, and oiled them, washed them, and bathed them.

170
00:12:48,359 --> 00:12:53,220
So, they came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rasool Ullah hug them and tears were swelling in his eyes.

171
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:55,379
So, Asma(أسماء) said: Something happened.

172
00:12:55,609 --> 00:12:58,180
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Yes Jafar(جعفر) was killed,

173
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:01,616
She screamed when she heard the news

174
00:13:02,066 --> 00:13:07,329
and Rasool Allah ﷺ told her that I am their Wali(ولي) in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Aakhira(آخرة),

175
00:13:08,097 --> 00:13:11,728
I'm their friend in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Aakhira(آخرة), and I will take care of them in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and Aakhira(آخرة).

176
00:13:12,756 --> 00:13:17,035
This is an honor for the children of Jafar Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

177
00:13:17,593 --> 00:13:20,298
There's some lines of poetry, Asma(أسماء) said;

178
00:13:20,347 --> 00:13:23,517
lamenting the loss of her husband, Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفرابن ابي طالب).

179
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:25,103
Asma Bint Umais(أسماء بنت عميس) said;

180
00:13:25,127 --> 00:13:28,415
فَآلَيْتُ لَا تَنْفَكُّ نَفْسِيْ حَزِيْنَةً

181
00:13:28,713 --> 00:13:31,647
علَيْكَ وَلَا يَنْفَكُّ جِلْدِيْ أَغْبَر

182
00:13:32,006 --> 00:13:34,920
فَلِلّهِ عَيْنَا مَنْ رَّآى مِثْلَهُ فَتَىً

183
00:13:35,193 --> 00:13:37,991
أَكَرَّ وَأَحْمَى فِيْ الْهِيَاجِ وَأَصْبَر

184
00:13:39,069 --> 00:13:46,791
I swear my soul will never ceased to be sad over you, and my skin will always wear dust.

185
00:13:47,514 --> 00:13:53,380
No one ever saw the like of him, a hero, who persisted, so valiantly in the fray.

186
00:13:54,154 --> 00:13:59,755
These words of Asma(أسماء), show her sorrow over the loss of her husband.

187
00:14:00,408 --> 00:14:02,654
After the end of her Id'dah(عدة).

188
00:14:02,915 --> 00:14:07,630
The waiting period which the wife is required to have,

189
00:14:08,043 --> 00:14:12,007
after she becomes a widow, before being allowed to marry again.

190
00:14:12,980 --> 00:14:18,763
She was approached by Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) and she agreed to marry him.

191
00:14:19,330 --> 00:14:21,683
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was invited to the Waleema(وليمه).

192
00:14:22,523 --> 00:14:26,332
He asked Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) permission to speak to Asma(أسماء).

193
00:14:26,641 --> 00:14:29,974
Asma(أسماء) is the wife of his deceased brother.

194
00:14:30,373 --> 00:14:34,696
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) gave him permission, so Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) spoke to her from behind a curtain.

195
00:14:35,531 --> 00:14:39,133
He said: Who is the one, who said;

196
00:14:39,482 --> 00:14:46,297
I swear my soul will never cease to be sad over you, and my skin will always wear dust.

197
00:14:46,946 --> 00:14:51,510
He reminded her with her lines that she said about Jafar(جعفر),

198
00:14:52,014 --> 00:14:55,567
because here, she says that I will continue being sad for you

199
00:14:55,607 --> 00:14:58,845
and now you're she is getting married to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

200
00:14:59,501 --> 00:15:02,774
She said, Away with you Abul-Hassan(ابوالحسن) you are always joking.

201
00:15:03,668 --> 00:15:07,854
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had a child from Asma(اسماء), Muhammad(محمد).

202
00:15:08,397 --> 00:15:14,184
And then when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) died, Asma Bint Umais(أسماء بنت عميس) married Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

203
00:15:14,708 --> 00:15:19,824
So, Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr(محمد ابن ابي بكر) was brought up in the house of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

204
00:15:20,266 --> 00:15:22,731
And they had a very strong relationship

205
00:15:22,756 --> 00:15:28,041
and Muhammad(محمد) was a staunch supporter of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

206
00:15:28,674 --> 00:15:33,308
and he became a governor for Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) over Egypt

207
00:15:34,111 --> 00:15:37,393
and then later on, in the events that occurred after that

208
00:15:37,449 --> 00:15:42,594
in the war between Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Bannu Ummayyah(بنوأمية) Egypt fell

209
00:15:42,915 --> 00:15:49,006
and Muhammad Ibn Abi Bakr(محمد ابن ابي بكر) was chased down to Saeed Misr(سعيد مصر), where he was eventually killed.

210
00:15:49,693 --> 00:15:54,834
But until the end he was a defender of Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه.

211
00:15:55,517 --> 00:15:59,976
One thing to notice over here, is that with the early Muslims,

212
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:03,679
no Muslim sister will be left behind.

213
00:16:04,469 --> 00:16:10,146
If she's divorced she would be married, if she is widowed she would be married,

214
00:16:10,415 --> 00:16:14,087
they would not leave a Muslim sister alone.

215
00:16:14,818 --> 00:16:23,847
And this tradition cannot be revived, except if polygamy is promoted and accepted.

216
00:16:24,656 --> 00:16:29,060
It is important for every Muslim man and woman to be part of the family.

217
00:16:29,814 --> 00:16:32,696
That is part of our makeup to be part of a family.

218
00:16:33,247 --> 00:16:39,821
So, the Muslims in those days, they would marry a Muslim sister whether she's divorced,

219
00:16:39,893 --> 00:16:45,189
they would marry her, if she's widowed, they would marry her, if she's old.

220
00:16:46,169 --> 00:16:51,333
Now, we have so much Tabaw'wa'a(تبوعه) about, a lot of issues,

221
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:55,128
first of all polygamy has become unacceptable,

222
00:16:55,629 --> 00:17:01,426
marring an older sister is something that, many brothers see as unacceptable,

223
00:17:01,782 --> 00:17:06,598
married a woman who is divorced or widowed is also avoided,

224
00:17:06,847 --> 00:17:13,104
and this is not the proper, acceptable social life for Muslims.

225
00:17:14,116 --> 00:17:18,777
The, three commanders Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) let's talk about them a little bit.

226
00:17:19,695 --> 00:17:23,046
The first one Zaid Bin Harrissa رضي الله عنه.

227
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:26,554
Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) is from the tribe of Qudha'a(قضاعة),

228
00:17:26,981 --> 00:17:31,610
Qudha'a(قضاعة) is a Yemeni tribe that moved into Hijaaz(حجاز) and moved into Ash-sham(ألشام).

229
00:17:32,394 --> 00:17:36,531
He was taken by his mother to visit her family,

230
00:17:37,159 --> 00:17:43,397
and they were attacked ambushed by horsemen from Bilqeen(بلقين) another Arab tribe.

231
00:17:44,116 --> 00:17:47,810
So, they took them as slaves and sold them.

232
00:17:47,835 --> 00:17:52,686
I mean that's how it is, in the wild life of pre Islamic Arabia.

233
00:17:53,149 --> 00:17:55,355
They raids and they would take the families

234
00:17:55,379 --> 00:17:57,407
and take the children and just sell them in the market.

235
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,673
So, Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), they ended up being sold,

236
00:18:00,999 --> 00:18:07,989
Hakeem Ibn Hizaam(حكيم إبن حزام) bought him and gave him as a gift to Khadeejah(خديجه), the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

237
00:18:08,029 --> 00:18:10,496
 and she gave him as a gift to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

238
00:18:10,685 --> 00:18:15,375
So, Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) ended up in the property of Muhammadﷺ in the time of Jahilliyah(جاهلية).

239
00:18:15,643 --> 00:18:16,836
This is before Prophethood.

240
00:18:17,083 --> 00:18:19,750
Rasool Allah ﷺ loved Zaid(زيد), so much.

241
00:18:20,034 --> 00:18:23,728
The father of Zaid(زيد) and his uncle, they knew about his where about,

242
00:18:23,753 --> 00:18:29,305
so they came asking Rasool Allah ﷺ to give them, their son back.

243
00:18:29,901 --> 00:18:34,727
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them fine, how about we give Zaid(زيد), the choice.

244
00:18:35,583 --> 00:18:37,295
Let's leave it to Zaid(زيد).

245
00:18:37,628 --> 00:18:41,103
Zaid(زيد) now is an adult, he can make the choice for himself.

246
00:18:41,839 --> 00:18:46,470
His father was very happy with this, I mean definitely is going to choose us, over slavery.

247
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,735
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Zaid(زيد), Who do you want to stay with.

248
00:18:49,759 --> 00:18:52,425
Zaid(زيد) said: "I want to stay with you." Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

249
00:18:52,937 --> 00:19:00,756
I mean this tells us, volumes about the personality and character of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

250
00:19:01,253 --> 00:19:06,127
Zaid(زيد) would rather stay with Rasool Ullah as a slave, then go back with his father.

251
00:19:06,936 --> 00:19:12,931
Rasool Allah ﷺ, immediately said and I free you, and I adopt you as my own son.

252
00:19:13,212 --> 00:19:16,374
And from now on, your name is Zaid Bin Muhammad(زيد بن محمد) and not Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه),

253
00:19:17,055 --> 00:19:18,855
Rasool Allah ﷺ loved him so much.

254
00:19:19,336 --> 00:19:25,153
And he married him to Umm Aimen(أم أيمن), who also was a slave woman,

255
00:19:25,626 --> 00:19:30,950
Rasool Allah ﷺ married her to Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه) and they had the child Usamah Bin Zaid(أسامه بن زيد)

256
00:19:31,421 --> 00:19:39,129
and then Rasool Allah ﷺ married Zaid Bin Harissa(زيد بن حارثه), to his own cousin, Zainab Bint Jahash رضي الله عنها.

257
00:19:39,709 --> 00:19:42,881
We talked about this, the marriage did not work out, so he divorced her.

258
00:19:43,316 --> 00:19:45,397
Rasool Allah ﷺ said about Usama(أسامه).

259
00:19:45,766 --> 00:19:48,872
Because when Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed Osama(أسامه) to lead an army,

260
00:19:49,235 --> 00:19:53,322
some of the noble men were not very happy that

261
00:19:53,686 --> 00:19:59,187
Osama(أسامه) who comes from slavery background, should be the leader over them.

262
00:19:59,457 --> 00:20:02,563
Plus Osama(أسامه) was 18 years old very young in age.

263
00:20:02,947 --> 00:20:06,806
So, they talked about it a little bit, the news reach to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

264
00:20:06,854 --> 00:20:07,497
Rasool Ullah said;

265
00:20:07,553 --> 00:20:12,659
إنْ تَطْعَنُوا فِي إِمْرَتِهِ فقَدْكُنْتُمْ تَطْعَنُوْنَ في إمْرَةِ أبِيهِ مِن قَبْلِهِ

266
00:20:12,764 --> 00:20:18,652
وايْمُ اللَّهِ اِنْ كانَ لِخَلِيقًا لِلْإِمارَةِ، وإنْ كانَ لَمِن أحَبِّ النَّاسِ إلَيَّ،

267
00:20:18,803 --> 00:20:21,781
 وإنَّ هذا لَمِنْ أحَبِّ النَّاسِ إلَيَّ مِن بَعْدِه

268
00:20:21,976 --> 00:20:23,336
This Hadith(حديث) is in Al-Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

269
00:20:23,376 --> 00:20:24,533
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

270
00:20:25,154 --> 00:20:32,428
If you dispute His leadership, you were disputing the leadership of his father before him,

271
00:20:32,698 --> 00:20:38,142
and in the name of Allah, he is appropriate person for leadership

272
00:20:38,451 --> 00:20:41,980
and his father was an appropriate person for leadership.

273
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:46,825
And he is from among the most beloved people to me,

274
00:20:47,051 --> 00:20:51,648
and his father was from among the most beloved people to me.

275
00:20:52,878 --> 00:20:56,244
There's an additional virtue of Zaid Ibn Harissa(زيد بن حارثه),

276
00:20:56,631 --> 00:21:03,585
and that is, that he is the only companion mentioned by name in Qur'an.

277
00:21:04,057 --> 00:21:08,050
فَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ زَيْدٌ مِنْهَا وَطَرًا زَوَّجْنَاكَهَا

278
00:21:08,773 --> 00:21:12,964
He is the only Sahabi(صحابي) mentioned by name in Qur'an(قرآن) in the Surat Al-Ahzaab(سورة الأحزاب)

279
00:21:13,218 --> 00:21:16,306
in the book of Allah, that will be recited, until the Day of Judgment.

280
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:20,417
We are reciting the name of Zaid Bin Harissa رضي الله عنه.

281
00:21:20,647 --> 00:21:22,780
What a great honor for this man.

282
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:29,110
Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جعفر ابن ابي طالب), the cousin of Rasool Allah ﷺ, he is older than Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

283
00:21:29,451 --> 00:21:34,110
He made Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه) and he had some great positions over there.

284
00:21:34,344 --> 00:21:38,617
He was the spokesman of the Muslims with An-Najashi(النجاشي)

285
00:21:38,887 --> 00:21:42,248
and he was the one who would teach An-Najashi(النجاشي) about Islam.

286
00:21:42,791 --> 00:21:48,085
He participated in both Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه) and Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina.

287
00:21:48,363 --> 00:21:52,634
And when he arrived in Khaybar(خيبر), Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

288
00:21:52,896 --> 00:21:59,307
I don't know which causes me more joy, the opening of Khaybar or the arrival of Jafar(جعفر).

289
00:21:59,861 --> 00:22:03,369
And he is the one with two wings as we mentioned before.

290
00:22:04,050 --> 00:22:07,078
Abdullah Bin Rawaha رضي الله عنه, one of the Nuqaba'a(نُقَبَاء)

291
00:22:07,273 --> 00:22:12,430
who gave pledge to Rasool Allah ﷺ in Bay'ah-Tul-Aqabah(بيعة العقبة), he was an excellent poet.

292
00:22:12,847 --> 00:22:19,034
He has a lot of poetry in support of Islam and in defense of Rasool Allah ﷺ and praising him.

293
00:22:20,131 --> 00:22:24,123
There's a Hadith(حديث), I'll read this Hadith(حديث) to you,

294
00:22:24,385 --> 00:22:29,880
عن أبي أُمَامَةَ رضي الله عنه قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ

295
00:22:30,081 --> 00:22:35,138
بَيْنَما أَنَا نَائِمٌ أَتَانِي رَجُلَانِ فَأَخَذَا بِضَبْعَيَّ

296
00:22:35,486 --> 00:22:42,976
فَأَتَيَا بِي جَبَلًا وَعْرًا فَقَالَا : اصْعَدْ ’ فَقُلْتُ: إِنِّي لَا أُطِيقُهُ، فَقَالَا: إِنَّا سَنُسَهِّلُهُ لَكَ

297
00:22:43,571 --> 00:22:49,604
، فَصَعِدْتُ حَتَّى إِذَا كُنْتُ فِي سَوَاءِ الْجَبَلِ فإِذَا أَنَا بأَصْوَاتٍ شَدِيدَةٍ

298
00:22:49,882 --> 00:22:54,790
فَقُلْتُ: مَا هَذِهِ الأَصْوَاتُ؟ قَالُوا: «هَذَا عُوَاءُ أَهْلِ النَّار

299
00:22:55,653 --> 00:23:00,118
Abi Umaymah رضي الله عنه narrates, I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say when I was asleep.

300
00:23:00,645 --> 00:23:05,999
Two men came to me and they took me to a rugged mountain, and they told me: Climb.

301
00:23:06,023 --> 00:23:08,084
I said: I cannot, they said: We will help you.

302
00:23:09,064 --> 00:23:16,009
We heard some loud voices, screaming, and uproar, I said: What are these voices?

303
00:23:16,442 --> 00:23:20,304
They said: This is the groaning of the people of Hellfire.

304
00:23:20,973 --> 00:23:29,476
ثُمَّ انْطُلِقَ بِي فَإِذَا أَنَا بِقَوْمٍ مُعَلَّقِينَ بِعَرَاقِيبِهِمْ، مُشَقَّقَةٌ أَشْدَاقُهُمْ، تَسِيلُ أَشْدَاقُهُمْ دَمًا

305
00:23:29,898 --> 00:23:35,820
And then we moved on, and I saw people hanging from their tendons

306
00:23:36,504 --> 00:23:41,516
and their mouths are split open and blood is streaming out.

307
00:23:41,952 --> 00:23:43,555
 I said: Who are these?

308
00:23:43,819 --> 00:23:47,623
 قِيْلَ: هَؤُلَاءِ الَّذِينَ يُفْطِرُونَ قَبْلَ تَحِلَّةِ صَوْمِهِمْ

309
00:23:48,111 --> 00:23:54,379
They told me: These are the people who break their fast before the time, before the, right time.

310
00:23:54,949 --> 00:24:03,268
ثمَّ انْطُلِقَ بي ، فَإذَا أَنَا بِقَوْمٍ أَشَدَّ شَيْءٍ اِنْتِفَاخًا ، وَأَنتَنَهُ رِيْحًا ، وَأَسْوَأُهُ مَنْظَرًا .

311
00:24:03,796 --> 00:24:07,060
And then we moved on and I saw people who were bloated,

312
00:24:07,517 --> 00:24:14,405
and a stench would come out from them, a horrible smell and they had a very ugly Look.

313
00:24:14,839 --> 00:24:16,110
I said: Who are these?

314
00:24:16,755 --> 00:24:18,613
قِيْلَ: هَؤُلَاءِ قَتْلَى الْكُفَّارِ

315
00:24:18,906 --> 00:24:22,033
These are the killed from among the disbelievers.

316
00:24:22,396 --> 00:24:27,914
ثُمَّ انْطُلِقَ بِيْ فَإِذَا أَنَا بِقَوْمٍ أَشَدَّ شَيْءٍ اَنْتَفَاخًا ، وَأَنتَنَهُ رِيْحًا

317
00:24:28,183 --> 00:24:30,623
كَأَنَّ رِيْحَهُمُ الْمَرَاحِيْضُ

318
00:24:30,888 --> 00:24:34,698
 قُلْتُ : مَنْ هَؤُلَاءِ ؟ قِيْلَ : هؤلاءِ الزَّانونَ

319
00:24:35,029 --> 00:24:40,210
And then I saw many people who are bloated and stench would come out from them,

320
00:24:40,472 --> 00:24:43,343
and there smell was so horrible it was like toilets.

321
00:24:43,551 --> 00:24:47,806
I said, Who are these? They said, These are the ones who commit fornication and adultery.

322
00:24:48,498 --> 00:24:53,888
ثُمَّ انْطُلِقَ بِيْ’ فَإِذَا أَنَا بِنِسَاءٍ تَنْهَشُ ثَدْيَهُنَّ الْحَيَّاتُ

323
00:24:54,349 --> 00:24:56,027
 قُلْتُ : مَا بَالُ هَؤلَاءِ ؟

324
00:24:56,170 --> 00:25:00,464
قِيْلَ : هَؤُلَاءِ يَمْنَعَنَ أَوْلَادَهنَّ أَلْبَانَهُنَّ

325
00:25:00,664 --> 00:25:05,308
ثُمَّ انْطُلِقَ بِيْ فَإِذَا أَنَا بِغِلْمَانٍ يَلْعَبُوْنَ بَيْنَ نَهْرَيْنِ

326
00:25:05,348 --> 00:25:08,339
قُلْتُ : مَنْ هَؤُلَاءِ ؟ قَالَ : هَؤُلَاءِ ذَرَارِيُّ الْمُؤمِنِيْنَ

327
00:25:08,636 --> 00:25:13,209
And then I saw women and snakes were eating from their breasts.

328
00:25:13,526 --> 00:25:15,461
I said, What's wrong with these?

329
00:25:15,731 --> 00:25:19,757
They said: These are the women, who prevent their milk from their children.

330
00:25:20,082 --> 00:25:22,552
They don't breastfeed their infants.

331
00:25:23,009 --> 00:25:29,639
And then we carried on and I saw kids children playing between two rivers.

332
00:25:29,663 --> 00:25:33,427
I said: Who are these? They said these are the children of the believers.

333
00:25:34,306 --> 00:25:40,117
ثُمَّ شُرِفَ بِيْ شَرْفًا ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِثَلَاثَةٍ يَشْرِبُوْنَ مِنْ خَمْرٍ لَّهُمْ

334
00:25:40,355 --> 00:25:44,678
قُلْتُ : مَنْ هَؤُلَاءِ ؟ قَالَ : هَؤُلَاءِ جعفرٌ ، وزيدٌ ، وابنُ رَواحةَ

335
00:25:44,809 --> 00:25:49,391
And then we climbed a high place and I saw three men drinking wine.

336
00:25:49,534 --> 00:25:50,870
I said: Who are these?

337
00:25:51,009 --> 00:25:54,495
They said: These are Jafar(جعفر), Zaid(زيد) and Ibn Rawaha(إبن رواحة).

338
00:25:54,945 --> 00:25:59,714
And then we went to a higher place and I saw a three men. I said: Who are these?

339
00:25:59,843 --> 00:26:04,150
They said: They Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), Musa(موسى) and Eesa(عيسى) and they are waiting for you.

340
00:26:04,670 --> 00:26:08,514
This Hadith(حديث) was narrated by Ibn Khuzaimah(إبن خزيمه) and Ibn Habban(إبن حبان) and they are Sahih(صحيح).

341
00:26:09,698 --> 00:26:13,056
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), and we'll close with this statement, he says;

342
00:26:13,473 --> 00:26:18,019
فَالْمَجْمُوْع عَلَى الْقَوْلَيْنْ اِثْنَا عَشَرَ رَجُلًا وَهَذَا عَظِيْمٌ جِدًّا

343
00:26:18,305 --> 00:26:21,909
أَنْ يَّتَقَاتَلَ جَيْشَانْ مُتَعَادِيَانْ فِيْ الدِّيْنْ،

344
00:26:22,075 --> 00:26:27,952
أَحَدُهُمَا وَهُوَ الْفِئَةْ اَلَّتِيْ تُقَاتِلْ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ الله عِدَّتُهَا ثَلَاثَةُ آلَافْ

345
00:26:28,195 --> 00:26:32,412
وَأُخْرَى كَافِرَةٌ وَعِدَّتُهَا مائة أَلْفِ مُقَاتِلْ

346
00:26:32,555 --> 00:26:36,779
مِنَ الرُّوْمِ مائة أَلْفَ، وَمِنْ نَّصَارَى الْعَرَبْ مائة أَلْفَ

347
00:26:37,038 --> 00:26:44,161
يَتَبَارَزُوْنَ وَيَتَصَاوَلُوْنْ، ثٌمَّ مَعَ هَذَا كُلِّهِ لَا يُقْتَلُ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ إِلَا اثّْنَا عَشَرَ رَجُلاً،

348
00:26:44,351 --> 00:26:48,693
وَقَدْ قُتِلَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِيْنَ خَلْقٌ كَثِيْرْ، هَذَا خَالِدٌ وَحْدَهْ

349
00:26:48,920 --> 00:26:55,644
يَقُوْلَ: لَقَدْ اِنْدَقَّتْ فِيْ يَدِيْ يَوْمَئِذٍ تِسْعَةُ أَسْيَافٍ فَمَا صبرت فِيْ يَدِيْ إِلَّا صَفِيْحَةْ يَمَانِيَةْ،

350
00:26:55,802 --> 00:26:58,890
فَمَاذَا تَرَى قَدْ قَتَلَ بِهَذَهِ الْأَسْيَافِ كُلِّهَا

351
00:26:59,962 --> 00:27:04,484
دَعْ غَيْرُهُ مِّنَّ الْأَبْطَالِ وَالشُّجْعَانِ مِنْ حَمَلَةِ الْقُرْآنْ،

352
00:27:04,635 --> 00:27:12,245
 وَقَدْ تَحَكَّمُوْا فِيْ عَبَدَةِ الصُّلْبَانْ عَلَيْهِمْ لَعَائِنُ الرَّحْمن فِيْ ذَلِكَ الزَّمَانْ وَفِيْ كُلِّ أَوَانْ

353
00:27:12,838 --> 00:27:15,122
وَهَذَا مِمَّا يَدْخُلُ فِيْ قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى

354
00:27:15,146 --> 00:27:20,866
 قَدْ كَانَ لَكُمْ آَيَةٌ فِي فِئَتَيْنِ الْتَقَتَا

355
00:27:21,088 --> 00:27:31,908
فِئَةٌ تُقَاتِلُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَأُخْرَى كَافِرَةٌ يَرَوْنَهُمْ مِثْلَيْهِمْ رَأْيَ الْعَيْنِ

356
00:27:32,268 --> 00:27:37,813
وَاللَّهُ يُؤَيِّدُ بِنَصْرِهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ

357
00:27:38,051 --> 00:27:44,648
إِنَّ فِي ذَلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِأُولِي الْأَبْصَارِ۝

358
00:27:45,203 --> 00:27:46,922
So, according to these authorities,

359
00:27:46,962 --> 00:27:52,660
 the total killed should be 12 men these are the Muslims, who were killed in the Battle of Mu'tah(مَؤتَة).

360
00:27:53,214 --> 00:27:58,855
This battle that looked like a disaster, that look like an inhalation of the Muslims,

361
00:27:59,011 --> 00:28:01,029
only 12 men were killed.

362
00:28:01,133 --> 00:28:02,379
So, Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says;

363
00:28:02,596 --> 00:28:07,996
So according to these authorities the total number killed should be 12 men.

364
00:28:08,484 --> 00:28:11,971
Then he says that two armies of opposing faiths

365
00:28:12,280 --> 00:28:15,934
one consisting of those fighting for Allah's cause,

366
00:28:16,219 --> 00:28:23,274
and numbering 3000 men and the other of disbelievers totaling 200,000,

367
00:28:23,434 --> 00:28:27,709
100,000 Romans, and 100,000 Christian Arabs,

368
00:28:28,082 --> 00:28:34,660
 could battle together, with the resulting deaths of only 12 Muslims is truly great.

369
00:28:35,024 --> 00:28:37,888
And a large number of unbelievers were killed.

370
00:28:37,954 --> 00:28:42,240
Khalid(خالد) alone stated nine swords were broken in my hand,

371
00:28:42,391 --> 00:28:46,360
and finally only a Yemeni broad sword persisted with me.

372
00:28:46,583 --> 00:28:50,094
How many must he have killed with all those swords,

373
00:28:50,348 --> 00:28:54,816
not to mention all the other brave bearers of Qur'an like him,

374
00:28:55,030 --> 00:28:58,427
who sentenced to death, those crucifix worshippers

375
00:28:58,585 --> 00:29:03,731
upon whom be the curses of the Most Merciful at that time and forever.

376
00:29:04,105 --> 00:29:06,487
This relates to the words of the Almighty,

377
00:29:06,772 --> 00:29:10,161
there was a sign for you in the two sides that clashed,

378
00:29:10,375 --> 00:29:19,663
one side fought for Allah's cause, while the other were unbelievers whom they saw to be twice, as numerous, as themselves.

379
00:29:19,893 --> 00:29:24,126
Yet Allah assists with victory whomever, He pleases.

380
00:29:24,150 --> 00:29:27,955
There is surely a lesson in this for those who have sight.

381
00:29:28,129 --> 00:29:30,555
Al-Imran(ألعمران) verse 12.

382
00:29:31,073 --> 00:29:33,584
This is the end of Ghazwat Mu'tah(غزوة مؤتة).

383
00:29:33,624 --> 00:29:38,005
We move on to some Sarayah(سراية) that occurred in that year,

384
00:29:38,790 --> 00:29:44,944
there's a Sariyyah(سرية) lead by Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and this is the first appointment for Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص),

385
00:29:45,032 --> 00:29:49,220
you remember Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) became Muslim with Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

386
00:29:49,706 --> 00:29:52,616
So, he's just recently embraced Islam.

387
00:29:52,909 --> 00:29:59,703
Rasool Allah ﷺ very soon after their Islam put them in these positions of leadership because they were capable men.

388
00:30:00,343 --> 00:30:05,243
I mean, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) were born leaders, they had the capability

389
00:30:05,583 --> 00:30:07,758
and Rasool Allah ﷺ recognized in them,

390
00:30:08,130 --> 00:30:13,122
and immediately started giving them this authority to promote the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

391
00:30:13,700 --> 00:30:17,763
This battle was called Dhaat-Es-Salasil(ذات السَلاسِل) because of the area which this occurred

392
00:30:17,908 --> 00:30:22,047
near to well or river or source of water called Dhaat-Es-Salasil(ذات السَلاسِل).

393
00:30:22,488 --> 00:30:27,919
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) he was sent into the land of Balli(بلي), this is an Arab tribe.

394
00:30:28,369 --> 00:30:32,114
They are his maternal uncle's, so Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him to them.

395
00:30:32,267 --> 00:30:38,784
However, they gathered a force to fight and because of the numbers of this force,

396
00:30:39,046 --> 00:30:41,173
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) asked for reinforcements,

397
00:30:41,221 --> 00:30:45,040
so Rasool Allah ﷺ sent him Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة), among some Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

398
00:30:45,412 --> 00:30:50,087
When the reinforcement arrived, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: I am the Ameer(أمير),

399
00:30:50,964 --> 00:30:53,874
Muhajiroon(مهاجرون) said: No, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) is the Ameer(أمير),

400
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:56,133
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: No, I am the Ameer(أمير),

401
00:30:56,173 --> 00:31:00,853
because Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed me to lead and you just came as a reinforcement.

402
00:31:01,427 --> 00:31:05,227
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) rather than argue on this issue.

403
00:31:05,698 --> 00:31:09,913
He said: The last advice that Rasool Allah ﷺ gave me is;

404
00:31:10,123 --> 00:31:11,876
فَتطاوعا فَلَا تَخْتَلِفَا

405
00:31:12,188 --> 00:31:15,404
Agree with each other and do not disagree with each other.

406
00:31:15,736 --> 00:31:19,916
And Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) was a very soft and lenient man, he said: You are the leader.

407
00:31:20,724 --> 00:31:24,848
At nighttime Amr Bin Aas رضي الله عنه had wet dream, Ihtalaam(إحتلام).

408
00:31:25,454 --> 00:31:32,862
When he woke up it was very cold rather than bathing and that is the requirement, he just made Wudhoo(وضؤ).

409
00:31:33,068 --> 00:31:35,841
Rasool Allah ﷺ was told about that, when they returned.

410
00:31:36,048 --> 00:31:40,055
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: I feared for my safety this water is going to kill me

411
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:43,960
it was very cold, so I took precautions for my safety

412
00:31:44,155 --> 00:31:45,754
and that's why I just made Wudhoo(وضؤ).

413
00:31:45,895 --> 00:31:50,898
Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled and didn't say anything, so some scholars use this as an evidence

414
00:31:51,355 --> 00:31:56,403
that if there is a risk and the water is too cold and the weather is too cold

415
00:31:56,720 --> 00:32:02,121
then one can make Tayam'mum(تيمم) or make Wudhoo(وضؤ), rather than bathing,

416
00:32:02,871 --> 00:32:04,461
because requirement is Ghussl(غسل).

417
00:32:04,778 --> 00:32:08,746
This is the Sariyyah(سرية) of Dhaat-Es-Salasil(ذات السَلاسِل).

418
00:32:09,387 --> 00:32:13,504
And then there is Sariyyah(سرية) of Abi Obaidah(أبي عبيدة) and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) mentions it here

419
00:32:13,852 --> 00:32:19,779
and he says I mentioned it here because Al-Bayhaqi(ألبيهقي), mentions it in this chronological order

420
00:32:19,893 --> 00:32:24,599
even though, this Sariyyah(سرية) must have occurred before Sulh-Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبية)

421
00:32:24,639 --> 00:32:30,688
because Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) was sent out to the Leyarsud Eera Quraish(ليرسد عيرة قريش)

422
00:32:31,379 --> 00:32:36,252
to spy on the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and we know that during the time of Hudaybiyyah(حديبية),

423
00:32:36,641 --> 00:32:39,976
there was a truce and now there's a truce, so how could this happen.

424
00:32:40,157 --> 00:32:44,202
Now, I don't recall if I have covered this Sariyyah(سرية) before,

425
00:32:44,242 --> 00:32:49,094
I'm sure I talked about it in one of my lectures but I'm not sure if it's in Seerah(سيرة) or not

426
00:32:49,215 --> 00:32:53,001
I repeat it here briefly, just because Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) mentions it in this position.

427
00:32:53,204 --> 00:32:54,545
They were sent to Saif-Al-Bahr(سيف ألبحر).

428
00:32:55,229 --> 00:32:59,656
And the appointment was to gather reconnaissance on the caravans of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

429
00:33:00,016 --> 00:33:05,426
they ran out of food, so Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) would give them one date a day.

430
00:33:06,038 --> 00:33:09,977
When this narration was heard later on, by one of the Taba'een(تابعين).

431
00:33:10,001 --> 00:33:12,858
He said: And what would one date a day do?

432
00:33:13,647 --> 00:33:16,237
The one who was telling them this story said;

433
00:33:16,733 --> 00:33:21,238
When the dates ran out then we knew the value of one date a day.

434
00:33:21,262 --> 00:33:24,783
Now, you're talking about what would one date a day, do for us.

435
00:33:24,807 --> 00:33:26,535
I mean, what kind of meal is that

436
00:33:26,867 --> 00:33:30,998
yes it's insignificant but we knew how valuable and significant it is

437
00:33:31,166 --> 00:33:32,958
when we ran out of dates and we had nothing.

438
00:33:33,556 --> 00:33:41,133
Qais Bin Sa'ad Bin Ubadah(قيس بن سعد بن عبادة) was with them, he borrowed some camels from one Mushrik(مشرك).

439
00:33:41,518 --> 00:33:42,968
He told him: I'm going to pay you.

440
00:33:43,357 --> 00:33:49,892
And he would slaughter for them five camels a day until, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) banned him and prohibited him, from carrying on.

441
00:33:50,279 --> 00:33:53,686
Qais(قيس) was very generous, Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) stopped him

442
00:33:53,726 --> 00:33:56,815
because he's going to put himself in big trouble Qais(قيس) didn't have any money.

443
00:33:56,839 --> 00:34:00,714
How are you going to pay back for all of these camels that he's slaughtering for us.

444
00:34:00,797 --> 00:34:02,341
 So, he stopped him, by force.

445
00:34:03,193 --> 00:34:04,134
Now, they had nothing.

446
00:34:04,531 --> 00:34:07,927
Allahعَزّوجَلّ because these men are Mujahideen(مجاهدين) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

447
00:34:07,975 --> 00:34:10,496
Allahعَزّوجَلّ provided them with Rizq(رزق).

448
00:34:10,883 --> 00:34:15,000
They saw what appeared like a hill, a hill of sand, a sandone.

449
00:34:15,603 --> 00:34:19,788
When they came close, it was a whale, a dead whale.

450
00:34:20,441 --> 00:34:22,586
They said: We cannot eat from this because it's dead.

451
00:34:23,192 --> 00:34:28,138
And then Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) told them; We are the messengers of the Messenger of Allah.

452
00:34:28,237 --> 00:34:33,894
We are Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) and it is a necessity, so let's eat from it.

453
00:34:34,633 --> 00:34:37,898
They were very hungry and they started eating from this whale.

454
00:34:38,543 --> 00:34:43,028
In fact, what they did they set camp right there next to the whale,

455
00:34:43,517 --> 00:34:48,180
for an entire month, feeding off this whale.

456
00:34:49,140 --> 00:34:51,098
Every day they would eat from it.

457
00:34:51,689 --> 00:34:55,833
One of them said, Until the flesh on our stomach started to fold

458
00:34:56,243 --> 00:35:00,187
meaning their stomachs were so tight, tummies were so tight

459
00:35:00,227 --> 00:35:07,593
because first of all they were very fit and then also they suffered a certain period of malnutrition

460
00:35:07,618 --> 00:35:12,224
because of having no food for some time and in the desert, very exhausted.

461
00:35:12,435 --> 00:35:17,020
Now, they were eating every day daily, they're eating meat, meat, meat, from this whale

462
00:35:17,431 --> 00:35:19,898
until, the flesh on their stomach started to fold again.

463
00:35:21,192 --> 00:35:22,359
How many were they?

464
00:35:23,004 --> 00:35:26,372
Listen here, they were eating for an entire month and how many were they?

465
00:35:27,136 --> 00:35:32,786
Three Hundred, 300 men eating daily, this must have been a huge whale

466
00:35:33,111 --> 00:35:36,729
sperm whale or a blue whale Allah Ho-Alam(الله اعلم) but it was one of those big whales.

467
00:35:37,388 --> 00:35:40,232
Abu Obaidah(ابوعبيدة) wanted to do experiment with the size of this whale.

468
00:35:40,295 --> 00:35:46,128
So, he stood up a rib bone from this whale, and he had the tallest camel,

469
00:35:46,921 --> 00:35:54,543
and the tallest man ride on this tallest camel and go under this rib bone,

470
00:35:54,716 --> 00:35:57,386
which was set like an arc and it could not touch it.

471
00:35:58,074 --> 00:36:01,732
It must have been huge because camel is pretty high animal.

472
00:36:02,705 --> 00:36:09,626
And the narrator says we will tear out pieces of flesh as big as a bull

473
00:36:10,138 --> 00:36:12,707
and then they would, they would dry some of this meat.

474
00:36:13,762 --> 00:36:14,857
فَجَعَلنَا مِنْهُ وَ شَائِقْ

475
00:36:14,889 --> 00:36:19,032
They would dry this meat, they would cut off pieces, or slabs from this meat

476
00:36:19,094 --> 00:36:24,436
and just have them in the sun to dry, in order to preserve it otherwise it would rot,

477
00:36:24,907 --> 00:36:29,438
and they enjoyed their time very much next to this whale.

478
00:36:29,516 --> 00:36:31,806
Rizq(رزق) from Allahعَزّوجَلّ that was sent for them.

479
00:36:32,102 --> 00:36:35,224
When they went back to Madina, they told Rasool Ullah about this story

480
00:36:35,248 --> 00:36:39,096
because they had they had some doubt whether we were allowed to eat it or not.

481
00:36:39,820 --> 00:36:44,525
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: That is Rizq(رزق), that was sent to you by Allah

482
00:36:44,841 --> 00:36:48,521
have you brought some of it with you, so that I can have some of it.

483
00:36:48,751 --> 00:36:55,975
Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to have some of this blessed Rizq(رزق) that was sent to them by Allahعَزّوجَلّ

484
00:36:56,201 --> 00:37:01,792
and they said: Yes, and they gave some of it as a gift to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

485
00:37:02,637 --> 00:37:10,544
