He tells us to worship Allah alone without ascribing divinity to anyone else.

677
00:52:19,967 --> 00:52:22,187
He tells us not to follow our fathers.

678
00:52:22,909 --> 00:52:28,811
He commands us to pray and to be truthful and chaste and kind to our fellow human beings.

679
00:52:29,620 --> 00:52:34,275
Heracul(هراقل) said: You have mentioned that he enjoys distinguished ancestry.

680
00:52:34,926 --> 00:52:37,720
And this is the case with all prophets and messengers.

681
00:52:38,725 --> 00:52:43,249
Since, you say that no one else among you has made similar claims.

682
00:52:43,568 --> 00:52:46,188
I cannot say that he is imitating anyone.

683
00:52:47,090 --> 00:52:50,593
You also denied that any of his forefathers was a king.

684
00:52:51,285 --> 00:52:54,369
Which means that he is not the claimant of a kingdom.

685
00:52:55,127 --> 00:53:01,304
You also say that he was not known to tell a lie before he came out, with this message.

686
00:53:01,910 --> 00:53:05,833
Well I know that he would not start by lying to Allah.

687
00:53:06,506 --> 00:53:09,458
You have stated that the poor are his followers

688
00:53:09,884 --> 00:53:12,971
and this is the case with all messengers from Allah.

689
00:53:13,244 --> 00:53:16,117
The fact that his followers are on the increase,

690
00:53:16,426 --> 00:53:23,106
again confirms a phenomenon which is always associated with true faith, until it is completed.

691
00:53:24,130 --> 00:53:30,267
You have also mentioned that no one turns away from his religion after having embraced it.

692
00:53:30,913 --> 00:53:36,390
This is a characteristic of faith, when its light shines in people's hearts.

693
00:53:36,963 --> 00:53:43,845
You also deny that he is treacherous and no messenger of Allah, was a treacherous person.

694
00:53:44,156 --> 00:53:48,730
You also said that he calls on you to believe in the oneness of Allah

695
00:53:49,035 --> 00:53:51,297
and to pray and to be truthful and chaste.

696
00:53:51,794 --> 00:53:58,233
If what you have told me is true then he will have the supremacy right here where I stand.

697
00:53:58,981 --> 00:54:04,821
I knew that his time was due, but I did not think that he would belong to your people.

698
00:54:04,995 --> 00:54:06,694
Had it been in my power,

699
00:54:06,970 --> 00:54:11,597
I would certainly have taken the trouble to meet him, and to wash his feet.

700
00:54:12,296 --> 00:54:19,124
In these words of Heracul(هرقل), we see the intelligence and we see the understanding of history,

701
00:54:19,502 --> 00:54:23,999
and understanding of religion, and understanding of the laws of Allah

702
00:54:24,235 --> 00:54:29,598
and understanding, to the distinguishing traits of truth from falsehood.

703
00:54:30,005 --> 00:54:32,061
Who is a true prophet and who is not.

704
00:54:32,558 --> 00:54:37,080
And then Heracul(هرقل) is saying something and he's telling these words to who?

705
00:54:37,279 --> 00:54:41,845
To Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), the man who was leading the war against Muhammadﷺ.

706
00:54:42,262 --> 00:54:47,148
Heraculus, the Roman Emperor himself is telling Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان)

707
00:54:47,324 --> 00:54:51,455
that if I meet Muhammadﷺ, I would wash his feet.

708
00:54:52,426 --> 00:54:56,601
Now, these words had an effect on Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان).

709
00:54:57,085 --> 00:55:00,926
The letter was brought, and was read

710
00:55:01,470 --> 00:55:08,104
From Muhammadﷺ, the Messenger of Allah to Heraculus, the great one of the Romans.

711
00:55:09,051 --> 00:55:12,001
Peace be to those who follow the guidance.

712
00:55:12,621 --> 00:55:14,687
I call you to believe in Islam.

713
00:55:15,249 --> 00:55:20,611
Adopt Islam and you will be safe, and Allah will give you double the reward.

714
00:55:21,306 --> 00:55:26,077
If you decline, you shall bear responsibility of the Aresiyeen(أريسين).

715
00:55:26,500 --> 00:55:30,111
The Aresiyeen(أريسين) as Ibn Hajar( ابن حجَر) says; Are the farmers.

716
00:55:30,484 --> 00:55:33,341
 The Romans were a farming people,

717
00:55:33,804 --> 00:55:38,590
so Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling him that you would bear responsibility for their disbelief.

718
00:55:39,622 --> 00:55:41,712
After the letter was read, Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

719
00:55:41,810 --> 00:55:47,009
فَلَمَّا قَالَ مَا قَالَ، وَفَرَغَ مِنْ قِرَاءَةِ الْكِتَابِ كَثُرَ عِنْدَهُ الصَّخَبُ

720
00:55:47,318 --> 00:55:56,185
وَارْتَفَعَتِ الأَصْوَاتُ وَأُخْرِجْنَا، فَقُلْتُ لِأَصْحَابِي حِينَ أُخْرِجْنَا لَقَدْ أَمِرَ أَمْرُ ابْنِ أَبِي كَبْشَةَ

721
00:55:56,579 --> 00:56:03,373
إِنَّهُ يَخَافُهُ مَلِكُ بَنِيْ الْاَصْفَرْ فَمَا زِلْتُ مُوْقِنًا اَنَّه’ سَيَظْهَر حَتَّى اَدْخَلَ الله عَلَيْهَ الْاِسْلَامْ

722
00:56:04,107 --> 00:56:08,364
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said, When he said, what he said and he finished reading the letter,

723
00:56:09,063 --> 00:56:12,910
the noises became loud, so we were driven out.

724
00:56:13,476 --> 00:56:16,372
I then told my companions when we were driving out.

725
00:56:16,602 --> 00:56:20,842
This Ibn Abu Kabsha(اِبن أبو كَبْشَة), this is the name that they used to call Muhammadﷺ with,

726
00:56:21,078 --> 00:56:28,472
this Ibn Abu Kabsha(اِبن أبو كَبْشَة) affair has got to the point where he even scares the kings of those of pale skin.

727
00:56:28,843 --> 00:56:35,195
Thereafter, I was convinced that he would prevail and eventually Allah drew me into Islam

728
00:56:35,444 --> 00:56:41,447
because he saw that, that the Romans themselves were worried about Muhammadﷺ.

729
00:56:42,896 --> 00:56:45,192
And the these are the People of the Scripture.

730
00:56:45,305 --> 00:56:48,022
These are the people who understand about Prophethood.

731
00:56:48,424 --> 00:56:51,365
Let's look at the letter and some comments from Ibn Hajar( ابن حجَر).

732
00:56:52,175 --> 00:56:55,703
What title did Rasool Allah ﷺ use to refer to Heracul(هراقل).

733
00:56:56,011 --> 00:56:59,353
He didn't say the Roman Emperor, he said: Azeem Ar-Room(عظيم الروم).

734
00:56:59,393 --> 00:57:00,646
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) says;

735
00:57:00,982 --> 00:57:07,331
فِيْهِ عَدُوْلٌ عنْ ذِكْرِهِ بِالْمُلْكَ اَوْ الْإِمْرَةْ ؛ لَأَنَّه’ مَعْزُوْلٌ بِحُكْمِ الْاِسْلَامْ ،

736
00:57:07,442 --> 00:57:11,005
 لَكِنَّه’ لَمْ يُخْلِهِ مِنْ إِكْرَامِ  لِمَصْلَحَةِ التألُّفْ

737
00:57:11,372 --> 00:57:16,801
He was referred to as, among the great one of the Romans.

738
00:57:17,437 --> 00:57:18,659
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) says;

739
00:57:19,135 --> 00:57:27,421
he was not given the title of King or leader because he is discharged, according to the rule of Islam.

740
00:57:27,624 --> 00:57:30,517
 Islam does not recognize his kingdom,

741
00:57:30,759 --> 00:57:36,326
and does not recognize his authority, and does not recognize the authority of any disbeliever.

742
00:57:37,000 --> 00:57:38,195
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) says;

743
00:57:38,711 --> 00:57:45,410
But he was given a title, a cordial title of the Great One of the Romans.

744
00:57:46,155 --> 00:57:50,240
And then in the letter it says; Peace be to those who follow guidance.

745
00:57:51,212 --> 00:57:57,064
اَلسَّلَامْ مَنِّ التَّبَعِ الْهُدَى مُحَصِلُ الْجَوَابْ اَنَّه’ لَمْ يَبْدَاِلْكَافِرْ بِاسَّلَامِ قَصْدًا

746
00:57:57,346 --> 00:58:03,863
وَاِنْ كَانَ لَفظُ يُشْعُرْ بِهْ لَكِنَّه’ لَمْ يَدْخُلْ فِيْ الْمُرَادِ لِاَنَّه’ لَيْسَ مِمَّا لِتَّبَعَ الْهُدَى فَلَمْ يُسَلِّمْ عَلَيْهْ

747
00:58:03,968 --> 00:58:06,523
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not give him Salaam(سلام) directly

748
00:58:06,738 --> 00:58:08,981
but said: Salaam(سلام) on those who follow guidance.

749
00:58:09,387 --> 00:58:14,156
And since they do not follow guidance than Rasool Allah ﷺ did not give them Salaam(سلام).

750
00:58:14,424 --> 00:58:17,951
And that is because Salaam(سلام) is not given to the unbelievers.

751
00:58:19,167 --> 00:58:22,787
And also Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) mentions that Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said;

752
00:58:22,811 --> 00:58:26,963
وَلَقَدْ رَاَيْتُ جَبْهَتَهُ تَتَهَادَرُ عرَقًا مِنْ کرَبِ الصَّحِيْفَهْ

753
00:58:27,530 --> 00:58:31,381
When he was reading, the letter of Muhammadﷺ.

754
00:58:31,405 --> 00:58:35,094
When the letter of Muhammadﷺ was read to Heraculus,

755
00:58:35,379 --> 00:58:41,016
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان) said: I saw sweat falling down his forehead.

756
00:58:41,762 --> 00:58:45,458
That was how heavy the letter of Rasool Allah ﷺ was.?

757
00:58:46,232 --> 00:58:50,217
He knew that, this was the truth, but he did not want to follow it.

758
00:58:50,792 --> 00:58:53,544
And there's a story that is mentioned in the books of Seerah(سيرة).

759
00:58:54,102 --> 00:58:59,535
That Heracul(هراقل) called his patriarchs and told them that we should become Muslim.

760
00:58:59,559 --> 00:59:03,330
This is the Prophet that we were fore told about in our books.

761
00:59:03,725 --> 00:59:09,878
And they all roared, and they became angry and then Heracul(هرقل) told them, calm down.

762
00:59:10,099 --> 00:59:11,797
I just wanted to test your faith.

763
00:59:12,488 --> 00:59:17,397
So, Heracul(هراقل) wanted to become Muslim but when he saw the reaction of his people,

764
00:59:17,667 --> 00:59:19,680
he told them I was just testing you.

765
00:59:20,160 --> 00:59:28,649
And in another narration it says; He was telling this to, the one who carried the letter.

766
00:59:29,233 --> 00:59:35,072
He told him if I knew that I would be able to reach to Muhammadﷺ I would have done so.

767
00:59:35,807 --> 00:59:37,563
But he feared for his kingdom

768
00:59:38,113 --> 00:59:45,936
and therefore obviously, his intentions don't help him because he did not truly become Muslim.

769
00:59:46,635 --> 00:59:49,254
This is the story of the letter to Heracul(هرقل).

770
00:59:49,561 --> 00:59:54,840
The next letter was sent to Kisra(كسرى), the Persian Emperor.

771
00:59:55,227 --> 00:59:58,663
And this letter was sent with Abdullah Bin Hudafah(عبدالله بن حذافة).

772
00:59:59,008 --> 01:00:03,432
According to one narration, the letter was read in front of Kisra(كسرى).

773
01:00:03,866 --> 01:00:08,422
In the Name of Allah, the Merciful, the Beneficent from Muhammad(محمد)

774
01:00:08,447 --> 01:00:14,600
the Messenger of Allah to Kisra(كسرى), the great one of the Persians.

775
01:00:15,351 --> 01:00:20,772
Peace be upon him, who follows right guidance believes in Allah and His Messenger

776
01:00:21,050 --> 01:00:27,497
and declares that there is no deity, but Allah, the only God, who has no partners

777
01:00:27,970 --> 01:00:31,793
and that Muhammadﷺ is His servant and Messenger.

778
01:00:32,070 --> 01:00:38,191
I wish to convey to you Allah's call, for I am Allah's Messenger to all mankind

779
01:00:38,515 --> 01:00:45,140
sent with the task of warning all those who are alive that doom will befall the unbelievers.

780
01:00:45,527 --> 01:00:47,935
If you submit to Allah, you will be safe.

781
01:00:48,211 --> 01:00:53,060
If you refuse you shall bear the responsibility for the Megians.

782
01:00:54,624 --> 01:00:55,794
Kisra(كسرى) was angry.

783
01:00:55,985 --> 01:01:02,041
He said; How dare, he write this sort of letter to me, when he is my slave.

784
01:01:02,552 --> 01:01:06,078
And then he ordered his governor of Yemen

785
01:01:06,282 --> 01:01:10,981
to send two able bodied men, to arrest Muhammadﷺ.

786
01:01:11,021 --> 01:01:18,674
Look at the arrogance and the pride and look at how they use to view the Arabs as their slaves.

787
01:01:18,698 --> 01:01:24,096
Since, they are not people who have a great kingdom like them.

788
01:01:25,085 --> 01:01:31,603
So, he sent this letter to Bazaan(باذان), who was a Persian ruler of Yemen.

789
01:01:31,627 --> 01:01:34,773
Yemen at that time was invaded by the Persians.

790
01:01:35,517 --> 01:01:45,219
So, Bazaan(باذان) sent two men one of them his name is Abaadaway(عباداوي) and the other one kharkharaa(خَرخَرة), to arrest Muhammadﷺ.

791
01:01:45,608 --> 01:01:50,163
 They did not march forth in an army, they just went alone.

792
01:01:50,761 --> 01:02:02,236
The reputation that, they had was sufficient, they did not need to show force and to go out with soldiers.

793
01:02:02,855 --> 01:02:05,672
 Just the two of them alone travelled.

794
01:02:05,945 --> 01:02:09,734
When they reach to At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف), they asked where was Muhammad(محمد)?

795
01:02:10,108 --> 01:02:16,322
They told them, he is in Madina and the people of At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف) and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were very happy,

796
01:02:16,362 --> 01:02:19,653
they said: That's it, this is the end of the Muslims.

797
01:02:20,676 --> 01:02:26,417
These two men, they came to Madina, they delivered their instructions to Muhammadﷺ.

798
01:02:26,469 --> 01:02:29,926
They said: Khusroo(خسرو), Kisra(كسرى), the King of Kings,

799
01:02:29,966 --> 01:02:34,025
Shahanshah(شهنشاه) has written to Bazaan(باذان), the king of Yemen,

800
01:02:34,631 --> 01:02:37,568
commanding him to send us to take you, to him.

801
01:02:37,933 --> 01:02:44,546
If you comply, Bazaan(باذان) will write to the King of Kings, interceding on your behalf.

802
01:02:45,238 --> 01:02:47,672
This will spare you a great deal of trouble.

803
01:02:47,855 --> 01:02:51,486
 If you reject his order, you know how powerful he is?

804
01:02:51,799 --> 01:02:56,332
He is sure to destroy you and your people, as well as your country.

805
01:02:57,371 --> 01:03:03,401
Rasool Allah ﷺ answered back and told them, who ordered you to shave your beard.

806
01:03:03,741 --> 01:03:07,949
They have, their beard shaven and Rasool Allah ﷺ disliked that,

807
01:03:08,071 --> 01:03:11,660
and they had long mustaches, so Rasool Allah ﷺ told them,

808
01:03:12,031 --> 01:03:14,673
who ordered you to shave your beards.?

809
01:03:14,792 --> 01:03:15,983
They said, Our Lord.

810
01:03:16,152 --> 01:03:23,256
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: But my Lord has commanded me to wear a beard and to trim my mustache.

811
01:03:23,874 --> 01:03:27,052
And then he told them to wait until, the next day.

812
01:03:27,360 --> 01:03:28,741
This particular narration here,

813
01:03:28,766 --> 01:03:31,721
is the narration from Seerah(سيرة) and it's not the narration from Hadith(حديث).

814
01:03:32,302 --> 01:03:36,087
Next day when they came Rasool Allah ﷺ told them.

815
01:03:36,227 --> 01:03:38,952
اِنَّ رَبِّيْ قَدْ قَتَلَ رَبَّكُمْ الَّيْلَ

816
01:03:39,222 --> 01:03:42,797
My Lord has killed your lord this night.

817
01:03:43,723 --> 01:03:46,540
They said: Do you realize, what you're saying,

818
01:03:46,829 --> 01:03:52,064
your arrest has been ordered for something much more trivial, than this.

819
01:03:52,298 --> 01:03:57,599
Do you still wish us to write this down and inform King Badaan(باذان) of what you have just said.?

820
01:03:58,345 --> 01:03:59,911
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

821
01:04:00,236 --> 01:04:09,803
Tell him, also on my behalf that my religion and my kingdom will replace that of Kisra(كسرى) and will sweep all before it.

822
01:04:10,213 --> 01:04:17,310
Tell him also that, if he accepts Islam, I will give him what he has now under his authority,

823
01:04:17,658 --> 01:04:21,206
and will make him a ruler in the area, he now governs.

824
01:04:21,651 --> 01:04:24,609
And then he gave them a gift and ordered them to leave.

825
01:04:24,872 --> 01:04:29,448
Whenever, a delegation received the tradition is that you give them something as a gift.

826
01:04:30,310 --> 01:04:33,868
Like we just saw before they told Rasool Allah ﷺ what you're saying is very dangerous

827
01:04:33,893 --> 01:04:36,912
to claim that Kisraa(كسرى) has been killed is very dangerous.

828
01:04:37,402 --> 01:04:43,086
I mean, we have instructions to arrest you for something less, and this crime is very grave.

829
01:04:43,207 --> 01:04:47,591
Do you know the consequences of what you saying; Rasool Allah ﷺ told them; Yes.

830
01:04:47,639 --> 01:04:53,405
Go and, also go and tell him this, that my kingdom will take over his.

831
01:04:53,833 --> 01:04:58,477
They went back to Bazaan(باذان) and Bazaan(باذان) said; These words are not the words of a King.

832
01:04:58,501 --> 01:05:00,804
These are words of a Prophet but let's wait and see.

833
01:05:00,952 --> 01:05:05,859
Let's wait until, we see if there's any news that will reach about Kisraa(كِسرى).

834
01:05:06,387 --> 01:05:10,411
A while later, because it takes a long time for a message to be dispatched.

835
01:05:10,930 --> 01:05:16,036
A while later they received information that Kisraa(كِسرى) was killed the same exact night

836
01:05:16,334 --> 01:05:20,391
that was told by Rasool Allah ﷺ, Bazaan(باذان) became Muslim.

837
01:05:20,984 --> 01:05:26,004
He knew that, this was a miracle from Allah and this is Rasool Allah ﷺ, so he became Muslim,

838
01:05:26,274 --> 01:05:28,973
and that was the beginning of the spread of Islam in Yemen.

839
01:05:29,634 --> 01:05:35,997
This new Kisra(كسرى) that is now ruling, he's the one who killed his father.

840
01:05:36,402 --> 01:05:38,889
 He sent a letter to Bazaan(باذان) telling him,

841
01:05:39,309 --> 01:05:43,647
that I've killed my father because of what he has done to our noble men

842
01:05:43,963 --> 01:05:49,382
and I want you to stop doing anything regarding the Prophet,

843
01:05:49,995 --> 01:05:52,123
whom my father sent you a letter to arrest.

844
01:05:52,850 --> 01:05:55,209
Kisra(كسرى) when he received the letter of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

845
01:05:55,249 --> 01:05:56,868
 What did he do? He tore it apart.

846
01:05:56,892 --> 01:05:57,898
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

847
01:05:57,938 --> 01:05:59,429
مَزق الله مُلكا

848
01:05:59,708 --> 01:06:03,667
Allah will tear apart his kingdom and that is what happened.

849
01:06:03,999 --> 01:06:10,695
The Muslims conquered the entire kingdom of the Persian Empire, the Empire of Kisra(كِسرى).

850
01:06:11,353 --> 01:06:15,512
The next letter was sent to Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس), the ruler of Egypt

851
01:06:16,305 --> 01:06:20,004
and this letter was sent with Hatib Ibn Abi Balta(حاطب إبن أبي بلتى).

852
01:06:20,282 --> 01:06:21,207
The letter read,

853
01:06:21,560 --> 01:06:24,563
In the Name of Allah, the Merciful, the Beneficent,

854
01:06:24,941 --> 01:06:30,776
from Muhammad Ibn Abdellah(محمد ابن عبدالله) to Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس), the great of the Copts.

855
01:06:31,342 --> 01:06:34,749
Peace be to those who follow right guidance.

856
01:06:34,983 --> 01:06:39,864
I wish to convey to you the message of Islam accept Islam and you will be safe,

857
01:06:40,353 --> 01:06:43,602
accept it and Allah will double your reward.

858
01:06:43,745 --> 01:06:48,977
 Should you turn your back on it you will bear the responsibility for the Copts.

859
01:06:49,723 --> 01:06:55,659
People of the Book! Let us come to a fair agreement that we shall not worship anyone but Allah,

860
01:06:56,265 --> 01:06:59,514
and that we will never ascribe divinity to anyone else.

861
01:06:59,971 --> 01:07:06,813
And that none of us will give others the status of Lord alongside Allah.

862
01:07:07,395 --> 01:07:12,874
If they refuse, say to them, bear witness that we submit ourselves to Allah.

863
01:07:13,222 --> 01:07:15,538
Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس) said: I have questions for you

864
01:07:15,901 --> 01:07:18,472
and you'd like you to help me reach understanding.

865
01:07:18,750 --> 01:07:20,234
Haatib(حاطب) said, Please ask.

866
01:07:20,742 --> 01:07:24,625
Al-Muqaocus( ألمقوقس) said, Tell me about your master, is he not a Prophet?

867
01:07:25,520 --> 01:07:27,208
Hatib(حاطب) said: He is indeed.

868
01:07:27,869 --> 01:07:34,716
Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس) said: Then why if he is so, why did they not pray to have his people destroyed?

869
01:07:35,047 --> 01:07:38,294
Since, they evicted him from his country to another.

870
01:07:38,547 --> 01:07:39,722
He said: Since he's a Prophet,

871
01:07:39,771 --> 01:07:42,777
Why did he make Dua(دُعَا) to Allah to destroy the people of Makkah,

872
01:07:43,236 --> 01:07:45,977
when they have driven him out of Makkah.

873
01:07:46,427 --> 01:07:49,382
Haatib(حاطب) said: Take Jesus, the son of Mary

874
01:07:49,868 --> 01:07:52,599
do you not bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah.?

875
01:07:53,054 --> 01:07:54,987
Al-Muqaocus( ألمقوقس) said: Yes indeed I do.

876
01:07:55,483 --> 01:07:57,654
Haatib(حاطب) said: Well, what about him.?

877
01:07:57,908 --> 01:08:01,003
When his people took him and wanted to crucify him.

878
01:08:01,199 --> 01:08:04,245
Could he not have prayed for the destruction of his people,

879
01:08:04,500 --> 01:08:06,856
when Allah raised him up to the lower heaven.?

880
01:08:07,395 --> 01:08:12,475
Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس) said: You are a wise man, who has come from the wise man.

881
01:08:12,987 --> 01:08:16,466
These are presents I'm dispatching with you to Muhammadﷺ.

882
01:08:16,783 --> 01:08:21,295
And I am sending with you a guard who will conduct you to safe haven.

883
01:08:21,775 --> 01:08:25,277
So, his response was polite but he didn't become Muslim.

884
01:08:25,537 --> 01:08:32,192
He sent with Hatib(حاطب), according to some narrations two and according to some narrations three slave girls

885
01:08:32,414 --> 01:08:35,898
very valuable and precious slave girls from among the copts.

886
01:08:36,546 --> 01:08:43,034
One of them was Mariya(ماريه), whom Rasool Allah ﷺ married and she gave birth to Ibrahim(ابراهيم),

887
01:08:43,445 --> 01:08:46,076
the son of Muhammadﷺ who died in young age.

888
01:08:46,338 --> 01:08:49,416
The other one was given to Hassan Bin Thabit(حسان بن ثابت).

889
01:08:50,178 --> 01:08:56,782
And he also gave Muhammadﷺ his Baghla(بغلة), mule, her name is Duldul(دلدل)

890
01:08:57,090 --> 01:09:00,294
and he gave Muhammadﷺ  some other valuable gifts.

891
01:09:00,887 --> 01:09:03,430
These are the letters that were sent.

892
01:09:03,724 --> 01:09:06,497
There is also a letter that was sent to An-Najashi(النجاشي)

893
01:09:06,762 --> 01:09:09,394
and another letter sent to the king of Ghassan(غسان).

894
01:09:09,648 --> 01:09:15,859
These are the letters that Rasool Allah ﷺ sent to the kings in the surrounding area.

895
01:09:16,260 --> 01:09:18,817
And we have seen what the response was.

896
01:09:19,158 --> 01:09:20,706
The response was different,

897
01:09:20,973 --> 01:09:25,806
The response of Kisra(كسرى) was the worst and the response of An-Najashi(النجاشي) was the best.

898
01:09:26,087 --> 01:09:32,505
Since, he accepted Islam and then you have Heracul(هراقل) and Al-Muqaocus(ألمقوقس)

899
01:09:33,056 --> 01:09:36,042
They were polite but they did not become Muslim.

900
01:09:36,423 --> 01:09:38,844
 We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to benefit us all.

901
01:09:39,495 --> 01:09:44,930
وَصَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

